course: dictionary
lesson: 15711
title: Touched: five meanings in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. You find the right one by looking at the words around it. «I touched the hot pan by mistake.» Here touched means put your hand on something, so the clues are hot pan and by mistake.
explain: The same word can show feeling. «Her kind letter touched me deeply.» Touched here means you feel grateful and moved, because someone was kind. Ask yourself: is this about hands, or about feelings?
explain: Touched on is a different phrase. «The teacher touched on the history of the castle for a moment.» It means mentioned briefly, not held or felt. Read the whole phrase, not just the first word.
explain: In maths, lines and shapes can touch too. «The two circles touch at one point.» Then they meet, with no gap. Try the meaning in each sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found it.
fact: Touched is the past form of touch: touch, touches, touched, touching.
fact: Touched means put a hand or part of the body on something, or came into contact with it.
fact: Touched as an adjective means feeling grateful and moved because someone was kind.
fact: Touched on means mentioned briefly, as in «The lesson touched on rivers».
fact: Touched can also mean a little crazy, but this is old-fashioned and informal, so you will meet it mostly in old stories.
fact: Wash your hands after you have touched animals, raw meat, rubbish or the toilet.
fact: You have the right to say no if someone touches you in a way you don't like, and you should tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «I touched the hot pan by mistake.» What does touched mean here? | Ran away from the kitchen | Lost it in the sink | *Put my hand on it | Painted it red
exercise: «Her kind letter touched me deeply.» How did the writer feel? | Angry and loud | *Grateful and moved | Bored and tired | A little crazy
exercise: Mum says, «Wash your hands after you have touched the raw meat.» Why? | *Because germs can get onto your hands | Because hands need to be cold | Because soap is fun | Because raw meat is a game
test: «The teacher only touched on the history of the castle.» What does touched on mean? | *Mentioned briefly | Climbed on top of | Painted over | Argued about in detail
test: Your body is yours. If someone touches you in a way you don't like, what should you do? | *Say no and tell a trusted adult | Touch them back | Keep it a secret forever | Let them carry on so they won't be cross
exam: «The two circles touch at one point.» What does touch mean in maths? | They are the same colour | They spin around each other | They are far apart with a big gap | *They meet at one point with no gap
